<title>UK: Novorossiisk closed by threat of thunderstorm.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk closed by threat of thunderstorm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil loadings at the Russian port of Novorossiisk were suspended on Tuesday after a thunderstorm warning, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>The Black Sea port, which is the main outlet for Russian Urals crude exports, was closed at 0930 local time.</p>
<p>A fairly strong southerly wind was blowing and the swell reached 1.2 metres, the source said.</p>
<p>The 145,000 tonne Sea Princess crude tanker sailed before the suspension was put in place, but the 80,000 tonne Prosperity and the 63,000 tonne Seawind 2 were both at berth.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
